{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"The disassembly confirms the cause: C’s unoptimized ABI sequence performs each addition with `b` as the SSE destination, while Rust vectorizes with `a` as destination; x86 preserves the destination NaN payload when both inputs are NaNs. I’ll encode the C operand order explicitly for `c2Add` on x86/x86_64, with a normal arithmetic fallback elsewhere."}}
